I am not doing any url syncs. I am normally getting the slugs from `this.props.params.slug` to find slug and use this in instantsearch like this in my `render()`

```jsx
<InstantSearch appId={ALGOLIA_APPID}
                apiKey={ALGOLIA_APIKEY}
                indexName={LOWESTINDEX}
                searchParameters={{
                    distinct: false,
                    filters: `slug: ${slug} AND instock: 1`
                }}>
```

When this slug changes, I need to get the new slug. 

```jsx
componentWillReceiveProps(nextProps) {
    if(this.props.params.slug !== nextProps.params.slug){
      
   // Change the state here.... and have Instantsearch take the new slug. 
    }
  }
```

I am not sure if I can provide a working jsbin example or not. If the above description is not clear, I can try to do it.

> Solutions to achieve this use-case: add a VirtualWidget with the slug param as the defaultRefinement.

This solution looks like a workaround (good one). But still in react I would expect that updating any prop on InstantSearch would actually do what I want: update the corresponding linked behaviors. What do you think?

Ultimately we might just have a state with:

```
searchParameters: {
  page: 0,
  filters: ...
  distinct: ...
},
widgets: {
  menu: {
    brands: 'Sony'
  }
}
```

But in the meantime, what about we allow updating searchParameters?

And users will be able to update any searchParameters (sorry this is confusing, I am not really talking about SearchParameters from the helper here, just all API parameters that are not handled by widgets.)
